4:["$","p",null,{"children":"The way we bake hasn't changed much since. Butter, never margarine. Vanilla beans, scraped by hand. Layers baked the morning they're collected — never frozen, never waiting under a fluorescent display case. If a recipe wouldn't pass Grandma Ify's taste test, it doesn't leave our kitchen."}]
5:["$","$L2",null,{"delay":0.14,"children":["$","blockquote",null,{"className":"my-10 text-center","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-script text-3xl leading-snug text-espresso-800 sm:text-4xl","children":"“People forget the napkins. Nobody forgets the cake.”"}],["$","cite",null,{"className":"mt-3 block text-xs font-semibold uppercase not-italic tracking-[0.18em] text-espresso-400","children":"— Ify, circa forever"}]]}]}]
6:["$","$L2",null,{"delay":0.18,"children":["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-espresso-600","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"Big bakeries will happily sell you a cake off the shelf. We start with a conversation instead — your grandmother's lemon curd, the song that played during the proposal, the exact blush of the bridesmaids' dresses. Those details become the brief, and the brief becomes buttercream."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Because dessert isn't the end of the party. It's the moment everyone leans in. We just make sure it's worth leaning in for."}]]}]}]
